<div class="page">
  <h1 class="page-title">About</h1>
  <p style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.7; color: var(--mystic-purple); font-style: italic; margin-bottom: 40px;">
    I help engineering organizations see what they already have clearly enough to build what comes next.
  </p>

  <h2 style="font-family: 'Libre Baskerville', serif; font-size: 1.2rem; color: var(--dusk-blue); margin-bottom: 12px;">The Work</h2>
  <p style="font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.8; color: var(--graphite); margin-bottom: 16px;">Fourteen years professional, twenty years writing Ruby if you count the kid who picked up RPG Maker in 2004 and ended up reading The Ruby Way two years later. I've been doing this long enough to know that the wider the scope, the more often the problem is people rather than code.</p>
  <p style="font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.8; color: var(--graphite); margin-bottom: 16px;">Most of my career has been in large, living codebases. Systems that grew because they worked, that got complex because the business succeeded. I've come to appreciate those systems. They represent years of hard-won knowledge from smart people making reasonable decisions under real constraints. The challenge isn't replacing them. It's understanding them well enough to help them evolve.</p>
  <p style="font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.8; color: var(--graphite); margin-bottom: 16px;">What I do is make the structure visible. I build the maps that show how things connect, who owns what, and where the friction lives. Once people can see the system clearly, they usually know what to do. The talent is already there. It just needs the right context to act.</p>
  <p style="font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.8; color: var(--graphite); margin-bottom: 40px;">I measure twice and cut once. If a meeting, a document, or a conversation can make something clearer, I'll drive to make that happen. If it's not clear to me, it's probably not clear to others either, and that's worth solving together.</p>

  <h2 style="font-family: 'Libre Baskerville', serif; font-size: 1.2rem; color: var(--dusk-blue); margin-bottom: 12px;">How I Work</h2>
  <p style="font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.8; color: var(--graphite); margin-bottom: 16px;">I match what exists. Whatever the style, whatever the context, I adapt. Clever code is hard to understand, difficult to debug, and hard to work with later. I aim for boring code whose intent is immediate and clear.</p>
  <p style="font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.8; color: var(--graphite); margin-bottom: 16px;">I wear different hats depending on what's needed. If I need to be code-heavy I will be. If I need to write a small novella worth of documents I'll start typing. I do what needs to be done and adapt to match the gaps I see.</p>
  <p style="font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.8; color: var(--graphite); margin-bottom: 16px;">I tailor information to altitude. Executives need distilled summaries. ICs need action plans. A lot of my time goes into translating between those worlds because that's where misunderstandings tend to live.</p>
  <p style="font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.8; color: var(--graphite); margin-bottom: 40px;">I'm autistic and ADHD. I write publicly about it. I can't sit still for more than an hour without mentally checking out, and sometimes need a few minutes between tasks while my brain reboots. I've built a career that works with how I'm wired rather than against it, and I think that's worth talking about openly.</p>

  <h2 style="font-family: 'Libre Baskerville', serif; font-size: 1.2rem; color: var(--dusk-blue); margin-bottom: 12px;">Ruby and the Ecosystem</h2>
  <p style="font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.8; color: var(--graphite); margin-bottom: 16px;">I've been part of the Ruby community for over a decade. I serve on the Ruby Central Board of Directors. I've keynoted RubyConf, spoken at RubyKaigi in Japan, and given talks at more conferences than I can count on both hands. I also lead a learning group of 500+ folks covering foundational Ruby topics.</p>
  <p style="font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.8; color: var(--graphite); margin-bottom: 16px;">My open source work started with a question: what if Ruby had pattern matching? I built a proof of concept. It got referenced in the core feature request. Ruby 3 shipped pattern matching. That same line of research led to AST tooling that powered automated refactoring across 27 teams at Square.</p>
  <p style="font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.8; color: var(--graphite); margin-bottom: 40px;">Now I'm building AI-native tools that understand codebases structurally. Not chatbots, but systems that know who owns what, what's connected, and how to help engineers navigate safely in code they didn't write. The goal is always the same: give people the context they need to do their best work.</p>

  <h2 style="font-family: 'Libre Baskerville', serif; font-size: 1.2rem; color: var(--dusk-blue); margin-bottom: 12px;">Growing People</h2>
  <p style="font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.8; color: var(--graphite); margin-bottom: 16px;">I've sponsored over 40 promotions across my career. Watching someone grow into a role they weren't sure they could fill is the best part of this job. I like to act as a shadow so other people's light is clearer and their value is recognized.</p>
  <p style="font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.8; color: var(--graphite); margin-bottom: 16px;">I co-chaired a neurodiversity initiative at Square because I believe teams get stronger when they're built for different kinds of minds. I sit on two university advisory boards and helped spin up a college CS program from scratch. Most of my family are teachers, so I have deep ties to academia and a belief that education changes everything.</p>
  <p style="font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.8; color: var(--graphite); margin-bottom: 16px;">I donate substantially to scholarship funds serving underrepresented groups. I've spoken in front of Congress on autism in education. I advocate politically, socially, and academically for autistic rights because someone invested in me early, and I want to keep that going.</p>
  <p style="font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.8; color: var(--graphite); margin-bottom: 40px;">The talent is always there. Sometimes it just needs someone to open the door.</p>

  <h2 style="font-family: 'Libre Baskerville', serif; font-size: 1.2rem; color: var(--dusk-blue); margin-bottom: 12px;">Outside Work</h2>
  <p style="font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.8; color: var(--graphite); margin-bottom: 16px;">I play too many instruments: classical guitar, piano, trumpet, french horn, and recently violin. I sketch buildings. I was a D2 college mid-distance runner and still run the occasional half-marathon. Always up for coffee if you're in town.</p>

